 hyperbolic conservation laws","volume":"27","author":"Sod","year":"1978","journal-title":"J. Comput. Phys."},{"key":"10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.113476_br0600","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"584","DOI":"10.1002\/num.10025","article-title":"Solution of two-dimensional Riemann problems for gas dynamics without Riemann problem solvers","volume":"18","author":"Kurganov","year":"2002","journal-title":"Numer. Methods Partial Differ. Equ."},{"key":"10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.113476_br0610","author":"Hendrycks"},{"key":"10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.113476_br0620","series-title":"Numerical Methods for Conservation Laws: From Analysis to Algorithms","author":"Hesthaven","year":"2017"},{"key":"10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.113476_br0630","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"439","DOI":"10.1016\/0021-9991(88)90177-5","article-title":"Efficient implementation of essentially non-oscillatory shock-capturing schemes","volume":"77","author":"Shu","year":"1988","journal-title":"J. Comput. Phys."},{"key":"10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.113476_br0640","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"76","DOI":"10.1137\/0524006","article-title":"Classification of the Riemann problem for two-dimensional gas dynamics","volume":"24","author":"Schulz-Rinne","year":"1993","journal-title":"SIAM J. Math. Anal."}],"container-title":["Journal of Computational Physics"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0021999124007241?httpAccept=text\/xml","content-type":"text\/xml","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/api.elsevier.com\/content\/article\/PII:S0021999124007241?httpAccept=text\/plain","content-type":"text\/plain","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,16]],"date-time":"2024-11-16T02:28:35Z","timestamp":1731724115000},"score":35.469402,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/linkinghub.elsevier.com\/retrieve\/pii\/S0021999124007241"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,1]]},"references-count":64,"alternative-id":["S0021999124007241"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.113476","ISSN":["0021-9991"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0021-9991","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2025,1]]},"assertion":[{"value":"Elsevier","name":"publisher","label":"This article is maintained by"},{"value":"Discovering artificial viscosity models for discontinuous Galerkin approximation of conservation laws using physics-informed machine learning","name":"articletitle","label":"Article Title"},{"value":"Journal of Computational Physics","name":"journaltitle","label":"Journal Title"},{"value":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.113476","name":"articlelink","label":"CrossRef DOI link to publisher maintained version"},{"value":"article","name":"content_type","label":"Content Type"},{"value":"\u00a9 2024 The Author(s). Published by Elsevier Inc.","name":"copyright","label":"Copyright"}],"article-number":"113476"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]],"date-time":"2026-10-09T07:50:48Z","timestamp":1791532248988,"version":"4.3.4"},"reference-count":39,"publisher":"IOP Publishing","issue":"5","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]],"date-time":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1791504000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":8,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]],"date-time":"2026-10-09T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1791504000000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":8,"URL":"https:\/\/iopscience.iop.org\/info\/page\/text-and-data-mining"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["iopscience.iop.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Mach. Learn.: Sci. Technol."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) can attain small residuals for partial differential equations while drifting from global invariants. We separate residual-based training from invariant enforcement: a standard PINN is trained first, and its output is then projected onto a selected invariant manifold at inference. The correction requires neither retraining nor a conservation penalty in the training objective. We derive explicit projection maps for the Korteweg\u2013de Vries and nonlinear Schr\u00f6dinger equations and for a mean-conserving Kuramoto\u2013Sivashinsky benchmark. Spatial field evaluation and quadrature are accelerated on a graphics processing unit, while one scalar update is computed for each evaluation time. Across these three one-dimensional benchmarks, projection reduces the selected-invariant violation by a factor of approximately\n                    <jats:inline-formula>\n                      <jats:tex-math>\n                        \n                      <\/jats:tex-math>\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" overflow=\"scroll\">\n                        <mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mn>1.1<\/mml:mn>\n                          <mml:mo>\u00d7<\/mml:mo>\n                          <mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mn>10<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mn>3<\/mml:mn>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <\/mml:msup>\n                        <\/mml:mrow>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/jats:inline-formula>\n                    \u2013\n                    <jats:inline-formula>\n                      <jats:tex-math>\n                        \n                      <\/jats:tex-math>\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" overflow=\"scroll\">\n                        <mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:mn>1.3<\/mml:mn>\n                          <mml:mo>\u00d7<\/mml:mo>\n                          <mml:msup>\n                            <mml:mn>10<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mn>4<\/mml:mn>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <\/mml:msup>\n                        <\/mml:mrow>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/jats:inline-formula>\n                    relative to the unprojected PINN, while prediction errors against the supplied numerical comparison trajectories change little. These results establish a benchmark-level post-processing correction over a unit time horizon; they do not establish long-horizon stability or generality beyond equations with a tractable scalar invariant.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1088\/2632-2153\/aeab20","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,22]],"date-time":"2026-09-22T22:51:30Z","timestamp":1790117490000},"page":"055035","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Two-stage projection physics-informed neural networks for preserving conservation laws"],"prefix":"10.1088","volume":"7","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-0537-5397","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xuewen","family":"Shen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Communication University of Zhejiang"},{"name":"National Radio and Television Administration Laboratory for Media Intelligent Communication Technology"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"},{"role":"conceptualization","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"software","vocabulary":"credit"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-3791-3460","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hanran","family":"Song","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Radio and Television Administration Laboratory for Media Intelligent Communication Technology"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"},{"role":"methodology","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"software","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-original-draft","vocabulary":"credit"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2186-3716","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Lipu","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Communication University of Zhejiang"},{"name":"National Radio and Television Administration Laboratory for Media Intelligent Communication Technology"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"},{"role":"conceptualization","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"formal-analysis","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"funding-acquisition","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"supervision","vocabulary":"credit"},{"role":"writing-review-editing","vocabulary":"credit"}]}],"member":"266","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,9]]},"reference":[{"key":"mlstaeab20bib1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"686","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jcp.2018.10.045","type":"journal-article","article-title":"Physics-informed neural networks: a deep learning framework for solving forward and inverse problems involving nonlinear partial differential equations","volume":"378","author":"Raissi","year":"2019","journal-title":"J. Comput. Phys."},{"key":"mlstaeab20bib2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1727","DOI":"10.1007\/s10409-021-01148-1","type":"journal-article","article-title":"Physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) for fluid mechanics: a review","volume":"37","author":"Cai","year":"2021","journal-title":"Acta Mech. Sin."},{"key":"mlstaeab20bib3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jcp.2024.112918","type":"journal-article","article-title":"Correcting model misspecification in physics-informed neural networks (PINNs)","volume":"505","author":"Zou","year":"2024","journal-title":"J. Comput. Phys."},{"key":"mlstaeab20bib4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1029\/2021JB023120","type":"journal-article","article-title":"Physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) for wave propagation and full waveform inversions","volume":"127","author":"Rasht-Behesht","year":"2022","journal-title":"J. Geophys. Res.-Solid Earth"},{"key":"mls